      "summary": "The logging processor clears unstructured messages only when there are no properties or scopes. A safe scope makes the record structured, allowing an already-rendered interpolated message to pass through unchanged.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Diagnostics/DiagnosticsSetup.cs",
          "line": 130,
          "message": "Interpolated log text can bypass redaction when a record has safe scope metadata, allowing credentials or other sensitive text to reach the exporter.",
          "confidence": 0.91,
          "category": "other",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "When a log record has a safe scope such as case.id, source.Count makes hasStructuredData true. For an interpolated message, data.Body already contains the rendered text, so RenderMessage finds no placeholders and returns it unchanged; data.Body is also left intact for export.",
            "failureScenario": "A caller logs an interpolated message containing a bearer token inside a scope with case.id. The processor preserves the safe scope, then exports the unchanged message body and formatted message with the token. OWASP A09:2025."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
