      "summary": "The log processor clears unstructured messages only when no properties or scopes remain. Safe metadata can make the record take the structured path, where an already-rendered interpolated message in Body is preserved.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Diagnostics/DiagnosticsSetup.cs",
          "line": 132,
          "message": "Interpolated log text can bypass redaction when a record also has safe metadata, exposing credentials or other sensitive text to the exporter.",
          "confidence": 0.91,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "RedactingLogProcessor treats any remaining property or scope as structured data, then renders data.Body without redacting it. For an interpolated log message, Body can already contain the rendered text.",
            "failureScenario": "A caller logs an interpolated message containing a bearer token while a safe scope such as case.id is active. The scope makes hasStructuredData true, so the processor preserves the rendered Body and the exporter can receive the token. OWASP A09:2025."
          }
        }
